{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-262949-r4615184","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Yogurt Curry Soup (Kadhi)","sourcePageId":262949,"sourceRevision":"4615184","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:34:31Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Yogurt%20Curry%20Soup%20(Kadhi)&oldid=4615184","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:29:26.986Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Gluten-free recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using chickpea flour","Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce","Category:Recipes using chile-ginger paste","Category:Recipes using clarified butter","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using whole cumin","Category:Recipes using yogurt","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Soup recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"bb05a9d97492d08797bbb0b49d574106ebb183da8c1633f59c6f11d871c751c3","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Curry recipes|servings=4–6|time=15 minutes|difficulty=2\n| Image = [[File:Gujaratikadhi.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Cuisine of India]] | [[Cookbook:Curry|Curry]]\n\n'''[[w:Kadhi|Kadhi]]''' also known as <i>Karhi</i> or <i>Gujarati Kadhi</i> is a sweet yogurt curry, normally eaten with unleavened flat bread called [[Cookbook:Roti|roti]] and [[Cookbook:Sabzi|sabzi]] in [[w:India|India]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Chickpea Flour|chickpea flour]] (besan)\n*1½ cups curds/[[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]] (dahi)\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ginger-green chilli paste\n*2 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]] (kadi patta)\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*2 tsp [[Cookbook:Clarified Butter|ghee]] (clarified butter)\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds (jeera)\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]] seeds (rai/sarson)\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]] (hing)\n*1 red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chilli]], broken into pieces\n*2 tbsp chopped [[Cookbook:Cilantro|fresh coriander]] (dhania)\n\n==Procedure==\n#Combine the gram flour, curds and 3 teacups of water in a pot. [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] well.\n#Add the chilli-ginger paste, curry leaves, sugar, and salt. Bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]].\n#Boil whilst stirring for a while.\n#Heat the ghee in a pan, add the cumin and mustard seeds, and [[Cookbook:Toasting|toast]] until light brown. Don't let burn.\n#Add the asafoetida and red chilli.\n#Add the seasoning mixture to the curry, and boil for a few minutes.\n#Sprinkle coriander on top and serve hot.\n\n==Note, tips, and variations==\n*This is a basic chickpea curry/soup. But, you can make its variations with [[Cookbook:Bitter Melon|bitter gourd]], [[Cookbook:Pakora|pakora]], [[Cookbook:Spinach|spinach]], and more. \n*Best served when hot.\n*This sweet yogurt curry is popular in [[w:Gujarat|Gujarat]] but in northern India, it is considered too sweet. So, prepare a variation depending on your guests' preference for spice.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Soup recipes]]\n[[Category:Gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clarified butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile-ginger paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Yogurt Curry Soup (Kadhi)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups chickpea flour (besan)","sourceText":"2 cups chickpea flour (besan)","amountText":"2 cups chickpea flour (besan)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1½ cups curds/yogurt (dahi)","sourceText":"1½ cups curds/yogurt (dahi)","amountText":"1½ cups curds/yogurt (dahi)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tsp ginger-green chilli paste","sourceText":"1 tsp ginger-green chilli paste","amountText":"1 tsp ginger-green chilli paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 curry leaves (kadi patta)","sourceText":"2 curry leaves (kadi patta)","amountText":"2 curry leaves (kadi patta)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tbsp sugar","sourceText":"2 tbsp sugar","amountText":"2 tbsp sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Salt to taste","sourceText":"Salt to taste","amountText":"Salt to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tsp ghee (clarified butter)","sourceText":"2 tsp ghee (clarified butter)","amountText":"2 tsp ghee (clarified butter)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"½ tsp cumin seeds (jeera)","sourc